      "q": "2. Expand the following products.\n(i) (3 + u) (v \u2013 3)\n(ii) 2/3(15 + 6a)\n(iii) (10a + b) (10c + d)\n(iv) (3 \u2013 x)(x \u2013 6)\n(v) (-5a + b) (c + d)\n(vi) (5 + z) (y + 9)",
      "a": "wer:\n(i)\nWe have, $(3 + u)(v \u2013 3)$\n$= 3(v \u2013 3) + u(v \u2013 3)$\n$= 3v \u2013 9 + uv \u2013 3u$\n$= 3v \u2013 3u + uv \u2013 9$\n(ii)\nHere, $\\frac{2}{3}(15 + 6a)$\n$= \\frac{2}{3} \\times 15 + \\frac{2}{3} \\times 6a$\n$= 10 + 4a$\n(iii)\nHere, $(10a + b)(10c + d)$\n$= 10a \\times 10c + 10a \\times d + b \\times 10c + b \\times d$\n$= 100ac + 10ad + 10bc + bd$\n(iv)\nHere, $(3 \u2013 x)(x \u2013 6)$\n$= 3(x \u2013 6) \u2013 x(x \u2013 6)$\n$= 3x \u2013 18 \u2013 x^2 + 6x$\n$= -x^2 + 9x \u2013 18$\n(v)\nWe have, $(-5a + b)(c + d)$\n$= -5a(c + d) + b(c + d)$\n$= -5ac \u2013 5ad + bc + bd$\n(vi)\nWe have, $(5 + z)(y + 9)$\n$= 5(y + 9) + z(y + 9)$\n$= 5y + 45 + yz + 9z$"
