      "q": "3. Puneeth\u2019s father went from Lucknow to Kanpur in 2 hours by riding his motorcycle at a speed of 50 km/h. If he drives at 75 km/h, how long will it take him to reach Kanpur? Can we form this problem as a proportion 50 : 2 :: 75 : ____? Would it take Puneeth\u2019s father more time or less time to reach Kanpur? Think about it. (Page 171)",
      "a": "wer:\nFirst find the distance: at 50 km/h for 2 hours the distance is $$50\\times2=100\\text{ km}$$. At 75 km/h the time required is $$\\frac{100}{75}=\\frac{4}{3}\\text{ hours}$$ which equals 1 hour 20 minutes. The form $$50:2::75:?$$ is misleading because the ratio of speed to time is not directly proportional in the way written; you must account for inverse relationship between speed and time for the same distance (higher speed gives lower time). So we cannot write $$50:2::75:\\frac{4}{3}$$ as a direct proportion of the same type. Puneeth\u2019s father will take\nless\ntime at 75 km/h (1\\(\\frac{1}{3}\\) hours) than at 50 km/h (2 hours).\n7.5 Sharing, But Not Equally"
