      "a": "wer:\nIf 3 buses carried 162 people when full, one bus capacity is $$\\frac{162}{3}=54$$ seats. For 204 people, number of buses required = $$\\frac{204}{54}\\approx3.78$$, so we need 4 buses to carry everyone. Total seats in 4 buses = $$4\\times54=216$$ leaving $$216-204=12$$ empty seats. So we need\n4 buses\nand they will not be completely full (12 seats remain vacant)."
