      "q": "3. In Question\u00a0 $ \\text{2} $\u00a0 above, if\u00a0 $ \\text{1} $\u00a0 part of a red pigment requires\u00a0 $ \\text{75mL} $\u00a0 of base, how much red pigment should we mix with\u00a0 $ \\text{1800mL} $\u00a0 of base?",
      "a": "Let us assume that\u00a0 $ a $\u00a0 denotes the parts of red pigment required. We know that parts of the base are in direct proportion to parts of red pigment.\nTherefore,\n$ \\dfrac{75}{1}=\\dfrac{1800}{a} $\n$ \\Rightarrow a=\\dfrac{1800}{75} $\n$ \\Rightarrow a=24 $ .\nHence, the table will be as \u2013\nParts of red pigment\n1\n24\nParts of base\n75\n1800"
