      "q": "6. In a model of a ship, the mast is\u00a0 $ \\text{9}\\ \\text{cm} $\u00a0 high, while the mast of the actual ship is\u00a0 $ \\text{12}\\ \\text{m} $\u00a0 high. If the length of the ship is\u00a0 $ \\text{28}\\ \\text{m} $ , how long is the model ship?",
      "a": "Let us assume that the length of the model ship is\u00a0 $ x\\ \\text{cm} $ . We can observe that the mast and length of the ship are directly proportional to each other. Therefore,\n$ \\dfrac{12}{9}=\\dfrac{28}{x} $\n$ \\Rightarrow x=\\dfrac{28\\times 9}{12} $\n$ \\Rightarrow x=21\\ \\text{cm} $ .\nHence, the length of the model ship will be of\u00a0 $ 21\\ \\text{cm} $ ."
