      "q": "8. Rashmi has a road map with a scale of\u00a0 $ \\text{1}\\ \\text{cm} $\u00a0 representing $$\\text{18}\\ \\text{km}$$. She drives on a road for $$\\text{72}\\ \\text{km}$$. What would be her distance covered in the map?",
      "a": "Given we have a road map with a scale of\u00a0 $ 1\\ cm $\u00a0 representing $$18\\ km$$. Let us assume that the distance covered by her is\u00a0 $ x\\ \\text{cm} $ . We can observe that the scale is directly proportional to the distance she covers.\nTherefore,\n$ \\dfrac{18}{1}=\\dfrac{72}{x} $\n$ \\Rightarrow x=4\\ cm $ .\nHence, the distance covered by her represents on the map as\u00a0 $ 4\\ cm $ ."
