      "q": "10. A loaded truck travels\u00a0 $ \\text{14}\\ \\text{km} $\u00a0 in\u00a0 $ \\text{25}\\ \\text{minutes} $ . If the speed remains the same, how far can it travel in\u00a0 $ \\text{5}\\ \\text{hours} $ ?",
      "a": "Let us assume the distance travelled by truck in\u00a0 $ 5\\ \\text{hours} $\u00a0 is\u00a0 $ x\\ \\text{km} $ . As we know that the distance traveled by the loaded truck is directly proportional to the time.\nTherefore,\n$ \\dfrac{14}{25}=\\dfrac{x}{5\\times 60} $\n$ \\Rightarrow x=\\dfrac{5\\times 60\\times 14}{25} $\n$ \\Rightarrow x=168\\ \\text{km} $\nHence, the distance travelled by the loaded truck in\u00a0 $ 5\\ \\text{hours} $\u00a0 is\u00a0 $ 168\\ \\text{km} $ .\nExercise 11.2"
