      "q": "8. A factory required\u00a0 $ \\text{42} $\u00a0 machines to produce a given number of articles in\u00a0 $ \\text{63} $\u00a0 days. How many machines would be required to produce the same number of articles in\u00a0 $ \\text{54} $\u00a0 days?",
      "a": "Let us assume the number of machines required to produce the articles is\u00a0 $ x $ .\nWe know that the number of machines and number of days are in inverse proportion.\nTherefore,\n$ 42\\times 63=x\\times 54 $\n$ \\Rightarrow x=\\dfrac{42\\times 63}{54} $\n$ \\Rightarrow x=49 $ .\nHence, the number of machines required to produce the same number of articles in\u00a0 $ 54 $\u00a0 days will be\u00a0 $ 49 $\u00a0 machines."
